1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,966
MyCampusView Academy.

2
00:00:03,016 --> 00:00:05,613
Robotics 101, video 13.

3
00:00:05,663 --> 00:00:09,410
Troubleshooting like an engineer.

4
00:00:10,550 --> 00:00:14,757
Real engineers spend a lot of time fixing things.

5
00:00:14,807 --> 00:00:16,060
That is normal.

6
00:00:16,110 --> 00:00:19,970
Here is how to troubleshoot like an engineer.

7
00:00:21,350 --> 00:00:25,252
First observe carefully: what exactly happens?

8
00:00:25,302 --> 00:00:28,172
Then make a guess about the cause.

9
00:00:28,222 --> 00:00:33,670
Change only one thing, test again, and write down what happened.

10
00:00:35,050 --> 00:00:38,902
If the robot does nothing at all, check the battery and the

11
00:00:38,952 --> 00:00:43,533
switch, check that every ground is connected, and make sure the upload

12
00:00:43,583 --> 00:00:45,120
finished without errors.

13
00:00:46,450 --> 00:00:51,628
If the robot spins in circles, one motor is probably wired backwards.

14
00:00:51,678 --> 00:00:57,310
Swap that motor's two wires and test each wheel with the motor test sketch.

15
00:00:58,650 --> 00:01:03,087
If the robot turns away from the line, the left and right

16
00:01:03,137 --> 00:01:05,369
sensors or rules are swapped.

17
00:01:05,419 --> 00:01:09,383
Swap the sensor wires on D2 and D3, or swap the two

18
00:01:09,433 --> 00:01:11,430
turning rules in the code.

19
00:01:17,650 --> 00:01:22,505
If the robot stops on a plain curve, both sensors may think

20
00:01:22,555 --> 00:01:23,752
they see black.

21
00:01:23,802 --> 00:01:25,665
They are too sensitive.

22
00:01:25,715 --> 00:01:30,570
Turn the knobs until white reads as white, then test again.

23
00:01:35,150 --> 00:01:38,125
The Serial Monitor is your best friend.

24
00:01:38,175 --> 00:01:44,640
If both sensors say BLACK over white paper, you have found the problem: calibration.

25
00:01:46,100 --> 00:01:47,414
Let us recap.

26
00:01:47,464 --> 00:01:51,609
Observe, guess, test one change, repeat.

27
00:01:51,659 --> 00:01:56,329
Most problems: wiring, calibration, or speed.

28
00:01:56,379 --> 00:02:01,573
Use the Serial Monitor to see what the robot sees.

29
00:02:01,623 --> 00:02:04,300
Next: The final challenge.
